  "sourceNotes": "Bohus Stickning was a Swedish cooperative (1939-1969) that produced garments using angora-blend yarn and a distinctive purl-stitch colourwork technique. The cooperative's patterns are no longer in print and the technique is now widely adapted. This is an original design inspired by the approach.",
