  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This Bohus-inspired mini hat is worked bottom-up in the round with a three-colour Bohus purl-stitch colourwork band in angora-blend DK yarn, fitting adult heads of 54 (56, 58) cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bottom-up construction places the signature Bohus band at head height. The distinguishing feature of the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "bohus-purl-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Bohus purl stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is that the rose-coloured (CC1) stitches are purled on the right side, pushing them forward from the grey background in a textured relief. CC2 stitches are knitted normally. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " method handles the full circumference. About 80 g MC + 20 g CC1 + 15 g CC2 of angora-blend DK yarn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Angora-blend DK yarn, MC (mid grey)",
              "qty": "80 g (approx. 175 m)",
              "substitutions": "Any DK works; angora adds characteristic halo"
            },
            {
              "name": "Angora-blend DK yarn, CC1 (deep rose)",
              "qty": "20 g (approx. 44 m)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Angora-blend DK yarn, CC2 (pale pink)",
              "qty": "15 g (approx. 33 m)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 8 / US 6)",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "3.5 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 9 / US 4) -- for brim",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch markers",
              "qty": "9 (1 BOR + 8 crown)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle and scissors",
              "qty": "1 each",
              "substitutions": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "22 sts x 30 rounds = 10 x 10 cm in stocking stitch on 4 mm needles. The Bohus purl stitches raise the fabric slightly and may pull in by 5%; check gauge in the colourwork pattern. At 23 sts per 10 cm the crown is 55 cm for size S."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Before you cast on, circle your size -- every count reads S (M, L)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast on"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on the 3.5 mm needle with MC, cast on 120 (120, 126) sts (multiple of 6). Tail formula: tail_cm = (needle mm x stitch count) / 10 + 15. For size L on 3.5 mm: (3.5 x 126) / 10 + 15 = 59 cm; round up to 65 cm. Join without twisting, place BOR marker."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 10 rounds of 2 x 2 rib in MC. Switch to 4 mm needle. After the brim, you should have 120 (120, 126) stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Plain body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 4 rounds of stocking stitch in MC only."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bohus band"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join CC1 and CC2. Work the 8-round chart, repeating the 6-stitch motif around. Where the chart shows CC1p: pick up CC1 and purl that stitch (right side facing). Where the chart shows CC2: pick up CC2 and knit. Where the chart shows MC: knit with MC. Float whichever yarns are not in use loosely behind. After 8 rounds, you should have 120 (120, 126) stitches. After the band, you should have 120 (120, 126) stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body to crown"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Break CC1 and CC2. Continue in MC stocking stitch until hat measures 16 cm from cast-on."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown shaping"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place 8 markers dividing sts into 8 equal sections."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Decrease round 1: *k to 2 sts before marker, k2tog; repeat from * 8 times. 112 (112, 118) sts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: knit all."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Continue alternating until 32 sts, then every round until 8 sts remain."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After the final decrease round, you should have 8 stitches on the needle, ready to gather."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Top finish"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut yarn with 20 cm tail. Draw through all 8 sts, pull firmly, fasten on inside."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common faults"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Purl stitches not standing proud: the CC1 purl was knitted instead. When the chart shows CC1p, the stitch is purled on the right side, which pushes it forward. That is the defining Bohus effect."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Three-yarn floats too tangled: when working with three yarns, keep each on its own bobbin or butterfly. Hold MC in the right hand and the two CCs in the left, or use a yarn guide to separate them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Angora halo obscuring the pattern: the purl stitches will still show even through the halo; the halo softens the edges. This is characteristic of Bohus work and not a fault."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. Block very gently over a bowl; angora-blend should not be aggressively wet-blocked as it may mat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash cool and very gently. Press out water without wringing. Dry flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Norwegian rose pattern hat uses a full all-over stranded repeat for a bolder colourwork statement."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}